{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118932","id":3581539622,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7VefUm","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118932","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118932.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118932.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118932","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118932/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118932/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118932/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/c0b714b07cfff7187435fce4cf77aab0231b345e","number":118932,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"dotnet: Make GodotSharp and generators compatible with trimming","user":{"login":"neikeq","id":7718100,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3MTgxMDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7718100?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq","html_url":"https://github.com/neikeq","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Depends on #116300, and #116301.\r\n\r\nThis PR makes GodotSharp and the Godot source generators compatible with trimming.\r\n\r\n**What this PR DOESN'T do:** This PR doesn't implement any logic for exporting games with trimming enabled. That can come later.\r\n\r\nEditor code still relies on unreferenced code reflection and dynamic code. All such paths are annotated with `RequiresUnreferencedCode` and `RequiresDynamicCode`. Managed callbacks had to be split between the ones that are trimmer-friendly and the ones that aren't compatible with trimming. The latter are only used by the editor.\r\n\r\nTypes with associated script paths now have to be registered explicitly from the entry-point (handled by source generators).\r\nBy their nature, those types are rooted (always preserved), as we don't know if/when Godot will need them. I added a `[NoScriptFileAssociation]` attribute to allow manually disabling this association for a type if not desired to not root it.\r\n\r\nTypes without an associated script path proved more complex. Explicit registration was a no-go because:\r\n- It gets complicated with projects where multiple assemblies declare script types (common with NuGet packages), specially if an assembly with scripts is a transitive (non-direct) dependency.\r\n- We don't want to root these types. They must only be preserved if they're used. But if they're preserved, their introspection/interop functions must also be preserved for Godot to be able to use.\r\n\r\nSo basically, we required a way to tell ILLink to preserve something as long as a type is also preserved. The solution for this was in the form of attributes, since attributes are never stripped from what they annotate.\r\n\r\nFor non-generic classes, the attribute implementation is simple:\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Click to see <b>ScriptTypeMetaProviderAttribute</b></summary>\r\n\r\n```cs\r\npublic abstract class ScriptTypeMetaProviderBaseAttribute : Attribute {\r\n    public abstract ScriptTypeMeta GetGodotClassScriptMeta(Type scriptType);\r\n}\r\n\r\n[AttributeUsage(AttributeTargets.Class, Inherited = false)]\r\npublic sealed class ScriptTypeMetaProviderAttribute<\r\n    // If this attribute is preserved, also preserve the public methods T.\r\n    [DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicMethods)]\r\n    T\r\n> : ScriptTypeMetaProviderBaseAttribute where T : IScriptTypeMetaProvider {\r\n    public override ScriptTypeMeta GetGodotClassScriptMeta(Type scriptType)\r\n        => return T.GetGodotClassScriptMeta();\r\n}\r\n\r\n// Usage:\r\n\n//  DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicMethods will preserve 'MyScriptType.GodotInternal.MetaProvider.\rGetGodotClassScriptMeta()'\n[ScriptTypeMetaProviderAttribute(typeof(MyScriptType.GodotInternal.MetaProvider))]\r\npartial class MyScriptType : Godot.Object {\r\n    protected static class GodotInternal {\r\n        internal class MetaProvider : IScriptTypeMetaProvider {\r\n                public static Godot.Bridge.ScriptTypeMeta GetGodotClassScriptMeta() => /* ... */;\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nIt gets more complex for generic types because you can't use generic type arguments in attributes. Thankfully, `DynamicallyAccessedMembers` works on strings that hold an assembly-qualified type name:\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Click to see <b>GenericScriptTypeMetaProviderAttribute</b></summary>\r\n\r\n```cs\r\n[AttributeUsage(AttributeTargets.Class, Inherited = false)]\r\npublic sealed class GenericScriptTypeMetaProviderAttribute : ScriptTypeMetaProviderBaseAttribute\r\n{\r\n    // If this attribute is preserved, also preserve the public methods of the type with this name.\r\n    [DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicMethods)]\r\n    private readonly string _nestedProviderGenericTypeDefinitionName;\r\n    \r\n    public GenericScriptTypeMetaProviderAttribute(\r\n        [DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicMethods)]\r\n        string nestedProviderGenericTypeDefinitionName)\r\n        => _nestedProviderGenericTypeDefinitionName = nestedProviderGenericTypeDefinitionName;\r\n}\r\n\r\n// Usage:\r\n\n// DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicMethods will preserve 'MyScriptType<>.GodotInternal.MetaProvider.\rGetGodotClassScriptMeta()'\r\n[GenericScriptTypeMetaProvider(\"MyGenericScriptType`1+GodotInternal+MetaProvider, AssemblyName\")]\r\npublic class MyGenericScriptType<T> : Godot.GodotObject {\r\n    private static class GodotInternal {\r\n        private class MetaProvider : IScriptTypeMetaProvider {\r\n            public static Godot.Bridge.ScriptTypeMeta GetGodotClassScriptMeta() => /* ... */;\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n### Backwards Compatibility\r\n\r\nAssemblies compiled against old versions of Godot use APIs that are not compatible with trimming. Additionally, some legacy APIs are rooted and waste a lot of disk space.\r\n\r\nTo preserve backwards compatibility and to improve trimming, I added the MSBuild property `GodotSupportLegacyNonTrimSafeAPIs`. This property is enabled by default to avoid breaking compatibility. Projects that don't have dependencies which use those legacy Godot APIs, can set this property to `false` in their **csproj**. Disabling this property makes the project trimmable, and removes the engine->C# callbacks\r that those legacy dependencies rely on, effectively no longer rooting them.\n\r\n### Some numbers\r\n\r\nThese results are for the [Squash the Creeps (3D) C#](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/d3337bbbe3dc2a75644eb5a0ee211f14f06e0dd5/mono/squash_the_creeps) demo project. Expect worse numbers on bigger projects.\r\n\r\nAs I said, there's no exporting logic yet, but we can follow some manual steps to verify the trimming results.\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary><b>The following lines were added to the demo's csproj</b></summary>\r\n\r\n```csproj\r\n  <PropertyGroup>\r\n    <!-- AOT build fails otherwise, because it doesn't seem to handle parenthesis characters correctly -->\r\n    <AssemblyName>dotnet_SquashTheCreeps3D</AssemblyName>\r\n\r\n    <!-- For warnings about trim compatibility -->\r\n    <EnableTrimAnalyzer>true</EnableTrimAnalyzer>\r\n\r\n    <IsTrimmable>true</IsTrimmable>\r\n    <VerifyReferenceTrimCompatibility>true</VerifyReferenceTrimCompatibility>\r\n    <IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>\r\n    <VerifyReferenceAotCompatibility>true</VerifyReferenceAotCompatibility>\r\n\r\n    <!-- Need to disable for compatibility with trimming without rooting. -->\r\n    <GodotSupportLegacyNonTrimSafeAPIs>false</GodotSupportLegacyNonTrimSafeAPIs>\r\n  </PropertyGroup>\r\n  <!-- For the rooted variant. -->\r\n  <ItemGroup Condition=\" '$(RootGodotAssemblies)' == 'true' \">\r\n    <TrimmerRootAssembly Include=\"GodotSharp\" />\r\n    <TrimmerRootAssembly Include=\"$(AssemblyName)\" />\r\n  </ItemGroup>\r\n```\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary><b>Commands</b></summary>\r\n\r\n- **Baseline (no trimming):**\r\n  `dotnet publish ./Squash\\ the\\ Creeps\\ \\(3D\\).csproj -r linux-x64 --self-contained true -p:DebugType=None -p:DebugSymbols=false -p:OutputType=Exe -o ./output_baseline/`\r\n- **Trimmed:**\r\n  `dotnet publish ./Squash\\ the\\ Creeps\\ \\(3D\\).csproj -r linux-x64 --self-contained true -p:DebugType=None -p:DebugSymbols=false -p:PublishTrimmed=true -p:TrimMode=full -p:OutputType=Exe -o ./output_trimmed/`\r\n- **AOT:**\r\n  `dotnet publish ./Squash\\ the\\ Creeps\\ \\(3D\\).csproj -r linux-x64 --self-contained true -p:DebugType=None -p:DebugSymbols=false -p:PublishAot=true -o ./output_aot/`\r\n\r\nTrimming is not possible (except in AOT builds) in library projects. The Trimmed variant uses `-p:OutputType=Exe` to be able to see the results, even though it would not be usable from Godot.\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nAdditionally, there are two sub-variants:\r\n- **Rooted**: Pass `-p:RootGodotAssemblies=true` to the command. It roots `GodotSharp` and the game assembly. This is how trimming was being done before this PR, so it can be considered a secondary baseline.\r\n- **SF**: Pass `-p:PublishSingleFile=true` to the command. It gives better results, so it's worth including.\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary><b>Results</b></summary>\r\n\r\n| Variant             | Size    |\r\n|---------------------|---------|\r\n| Baseline            | 80.0 MB |\r\n| Baseline SF         | 72.9 MB |\r\n| Trimmed (Rooted)    | 27.3 MB |\r\n| Trimmed             | 21.2 MB |\r\n| Trimmed SF (Rooted) | 20.1 MB |\r\n| Trimmed SF          | 14.0 MB |\r\n| AOT (Rooted)        | 21.4 MB |\r\n| AOT                 |  4.1 MB |\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\nThe most impressive results are for AOT, for which the whole thing (project and assemblies, and .NET runtime) only take up 4.1 MB with this project (expect worse on larger projects). This can be further reduced by [disabling framework library features](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/core/deploying/trimming/trimming-options#trim-framework-library-features) that the project doesn't need.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098009,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwMDk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:buildsystem","name":"topic:buildsystem","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":709269775,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MDkyNjk3NzU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:dotnet","name":"topic:dotnet","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":